1.1.text:
Article 3

(1) The objective of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence is to provide protection and services to victims of violence based on gender and the best interests of women and children occurring at home and/or in public places.

(21 Violence as referred to in paragraph (1)

can be in the form of: n

a. physical violence;

b. psychological violence;

c. sexual violence;

d. economic neglect; and

e. restriction of movement.

Article 2

The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of: a. respect for human rights;

b. gender equality and justice;

c. protection of victims' rights;

d. non-discriminatory; and

e. best interests of the victim.

Article 4

Every victim of violence has the right to receive: n

a. protection and assistance;

b. legal aid;

c. health services according to medical needs;

d. psychosocial services;

e. information; and

f. integrated services.

